This section documents the sink and water system installed in the van conversion.

## What Was Installed

- Sink and countertop area
- Fresh water tank
- Water pump
- Tubing and fittings
- Drain line
- Sealed sink edges
- Plumbing access points for maintenance

## System Overview

The plumbing system was built to support basic water use inside the van. A fresh water tank supplies the sink through a 12V pump, with tubing routed through the interior framing.

The sink, pump, and drain setup were installed with access in mind so leaks, fittings, and wiring can be checked or repaired later.

## Testing and Fixes

- Checked pump operation
- Tested water flow to the sink
- Checked fittings for leaks
- Sealed areas around the sink
- Adjusted tubing layout for better access

## Things I Learned

- Leave room to access fittings and tubing
- Test for leaks before closing panels
- Keep pump wiring and plumbing easy to reach
- Small layout changes make maintenance much easier
